      "card_ids": ["C02"],
      "claim": "The closest analogue, a benzimidazole-piperidine, showed a brain/plasma ratio of 2.7 after iv dosing, demonstrating that this core can achieve robust CNS exposure; the shared scaffold supports meaningful access for the query despite the added carboxylic acid.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C08"],
      "claim": "A related piperidine-benzimidazole/quinoline analogue showed a brain-to-blood ratio consistent with free passage across the BBB, reinforcing the CNS-penetrant nature of this chemotype.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C04"],
      "claim": "A structurally related piperidine ligand exhibited high and receptor-specific brain uptake in vivo, providing additional evidence that this scaffold can achieve meaningful CNS access.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    }
  ],
  "confidence": "moderate",
  "decision_summary": "The query shares a CNS-penetrant benzimidazole-piperidine scaffold with multiple analogues showing direct brain exposure (B/Pb 1.1-2.7 and high brain uptake). Although the carboxylic acid introduces a zwitterionic liability, the lipophilic gem-dimethyl acid and overall scaffold make meaningful CNS access plausible; the positive experimental evidence outweighs the physicochemical concern.",
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct brain/plasma or CSF measurement for an acid-containing analogue; all retrieved evidence lacks the carboxylic acid.",
    "No data on efflux transporter liability or active uptake for the query.",
    "Low Morgan similarity (0.28-0.39) limits quantitative transfer of the positive results."
  ],
  "new_evidence_assessment": [],
  "revision_action": "initial"
}

